# sha256 of every bundled file (tools/vendor_ashita_addons.py). Ashita-v4beta 877d9e76b65b0361706f9e2be3423a713f63d3c5
# left out: affinity: Windows-only: Win32 process CPU affinity
# left out: ahcolors: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: ahgo: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: autologin: built into the client: --char / --autoconnect and the launcher's profiles
# left out: cartographer: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: casper: does nothing: sets entity render flags, which the client does not read
# left out: chamcham: does nothing: writes model colours into actor memory the client does not have
# left out: chatfix: harmful: shifts LSB's chat packets by a byte for an old server layout, cutting messages
# left out: chatmon: does nothing: its feature is sounds, and addon sounds are not played
# left out: chime: does nothing: fails to load (the game's chime sounds are not mapped)
# left out: cleancs: does nothing: the font / primitive / ImGui managers' SetVisible is a no-op here
# left out: dynamic_entity_renamer: built into the client: dynamic-entity renames (LSB's spawn-name layout and HorizonXI's 0x1FF list) are handled natively
# left out: enternity: does nothing: edits log lines, but the dialogue box's wait comes from the event, not the log
# left out: fastswap: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: filterless: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: filterscan: crashes the client: calls game functions it scanned for (docs/ashita-compat.md)
# left out: freemem: Windows-only: SetProcessWorkingSetSize, a no-op here
# left out: hideconsole: Windows-only: hides Ashita's bootloader console, which the client doesn't have
# left out: hideobs: Windows-only: hides the window from OBS through SetWindowDisplayAffinity
# left out: hideui: does nothing: the font / primitive / ImGui managers' SetVisible is a no-op here
# left out: ime: Windows-only: the Windows IME
# left out: instantah: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: instantchat: does nothing: the client's chat log has no delay to remove
# left out: macrofix: does nothing: the client's macro palette has no delay to remove
# left out: mapdot: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: minimapmon: does nothing: controls the Minimap plugin, which the client does not have
# left out: mipmap: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: move: does nothing: moves and resizes the window through Win32 calls
# left out: nomad: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: noname: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: paranormal: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: quicksets: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: renamer: crashes the client: calls game functions it scanned for (docs/ashita-compat.md)
# left out: skeletonkey: does nothing: writes an entity's status field, which the client does not read
# left out: timestamp: built into the client: the native /timestamp and Config's chat timestamps
# left out: trimspells: does nothing: finds no stand-in for the game code it patches ("Failed to locate ... pointer")
# left out: truesight: does nothing: sets entity render flags, which the client does not read
# left out: watchdog: crashes the client: calls game functions it scanned for (docs/ashita-compat.md)
